{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/620855-need-tips-on-making-hunters-scary-to-be-stalked-by-if-you-re-a-monster","id":620855,"title":"Need Tips on Making Hunters Scary To Be Stalked By If You're a Monster","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-08T20:22:38-07:00","id":620855,"title":"Need Tips on Making Hunters Scary To Be Stalked By If You're a Monster","content":"Modern day Otodo, to be precise, but I don't mind in general.<br /> <br /> Seeing as how this is a Vigil board, I decided to ask for advice on how you, dear STs, have found how hunters have become nightmarish-not because they become worse than their opposition, but how they've shown how humans don't need a major template to make you feel powerless. I'm looking for a scene in a larger story where a bunch of misguided but noble Otodo/Lucifuge end up trapping a group of PC monsters in an unoccupied ship (think inverse <i>Monstrum</i>), and I want to make it clear that the PCs only options are escape or death-and the hunters are very persuasive about option number 2.<br /> <br /> <b>So, how do you make hunters scary in a &quot;hunting you&quot; sense?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 08-08-2015, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T21:42:42-07:00","id":620904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/620855-need-tips-on-making-hunters-scary-to-be-stalked-by-if-you-re-a-monster#post620855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Modern day Otodo, to be precise, but I don't mind in general.<br /> <br /> Seeing as how this is a Vigil board, I decided to ask for advice on how you, dear STs, have found how hunters have become nightmarish-not because they become worse than their opposition, but how they've shown how humans don't need a major template to make you feel powerless. I'm looking for a scene in a larger story where a bunch of misguided but noble Otodo/Lucifuge end up trapping a group of PC monsters in an unoccupied ship (think inverse <i>Monstrum</i>), and I want to make it clear that the PCs only options are escape or death-and the hunters are very persuasive about option number 2.<br /> <br /> <b>So, how do you make hunters scary in a &quot;hunting you&quot; sense?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Scary? depends. Play up the paranoia of being watched. You're under the microscope. You go home and find things missing or something just ever so slightly out of place.<br /> <br /> After that, start playing up numbers. Haha, puny human! I am attacking you and... holy shit! I am now dealing with six others! MMA fighters can best one person. Can hold off two at a time. but three and above? They run or get their asses kicked.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, Hunter cells can pull allies from uncommon sources. Use this card often. Favors can be called in from other Hunter cells or even some supernatural groups that the cell has done a favor for in the past.<br /> <br /> This is all on top research and legwork Hunters have done to prepare themselves for a certain enemy or supernatural.<br /> <br /> edit: and the last thing I want to mention is Hunters can go full crazy train down the morality meter should push come to shove. Supernaturals may get KEWL powers but Hunters counter by going with antics that makes a 40k inquisitor look tame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 08-09-2015, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:22:10-07:00","id":620936,"title":"","content":"I'll give you some quick examples. Please tell me if I should be clearer or more illustrative.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://img.4plebs.org/boards/tg/image/1396/90/1396906144287.gif\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Take cues from these guys.</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MookChivalry\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Do not assume monsters have a sense of fair play</b></a>. No trick is too dirty for either side.<br /> <br /> If burning, staking and decapitating an Elder Ventrue doesn't work, go after his money. Attack his resources at their roots, implant rumors, create false paper trails, lead him into bad investments, throw mud at his PR from the shadows and find out all you can about the dirt under his fingernails. Never give up the act, never let him know it was your cell's idea. Ask for the <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/wod2/htv/CompactBaC.html\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Barrett Commission's</b></a> help if you are out of options, but keep your eyes open. Have <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Realpolitik\" target=\"_blank\"><b>realpolitikers</b></a> a phone call or e-mail away at all times.<br /> <br /> Blame someone else if the shit hits the fan. If he doesn't buy it, lure his hitmen into the place you have been leading him to think is your cell's hideout, but is empty. Except for the spring-loaded wooden stakes, incendiary explosives and the cherry on top: a timed bomb version of the <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/wod2/htv/CreationMeAdA.html\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Bleeder</b></a> (VALKYRIE'S heavy laser cannon that microwaves the blood out of vampires in a very nasty way).<br /> <br /> Have a clean up team on hold to take care of whatever is left of the hitmen. No matter how influential the Ventrue is, there are only so many underlings willing to go on suicide missions. He'll eventually take the hint and go play chess master somewhere else. (Don't gimme that &quot;sunlight/torpor doesn't let him take an airplane&quot; nonsense. He can damn well pay a changeling to guide him through the Hedge or a mage to teleport him)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-09-2015, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T01:04:28-07:00","id":620966,"title":"","content":"This came up when I was talking about Endowments with PenDragon just the other day. These thoughts were more for PC hunters but I'll try to adapt them.<br /> <br /> Basically. What makes the players feel powerful, like predictors? Endowments target that and take it away.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Lucifuge are the royalty of hell and most monsters are just the lowly peasants. The thing about old school nobility isn't that they had a better sword. It's that the rules were stacked in their favour. They could hurt you, and the rules forbade them from defending themselves. Read about how black people were treated in Jim Crow south and try to recreate that feeling in the players. Perhaps the Lucifuge curses players to be attacked by their own sins. Then starts shooting, but every time the players shoot back <i>another</i> Wrath demon joins the fight against them.<br /> <br /> Vampire's are predictors who thrive in secrecy. Perhaps under the Lucifuge's curse they cannot feed without breaking the Masqurade. After stepping out of a quiet corner in the club they notice blood is spontaneously appearing all over their shirt, then the blood spells out &quot;vamprie&quot; and starts glowing and everyone can see them even though they're Obsurificated. They kill someone and turn the body over to the vampire authorities for disposal, only to be followed around by a ghost shouting murder.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T13:54:48-07:00","id":621611,"title":"","content":"The scariest thing hunters do is <b>plan</b>.<br /> <br /> Near the beginning of the scene, right before/as they're getting onto that ship have the hunt's plan proceed like a fine-tuned machine; escape is cut off, banes are brought into play, there's a hint that research has been done. The player characters are stuck reacting to something the hunters have already gamed out.<br /> <br /> Then pull it back. Maybe part of the hunter's plan goes awry and they have to regroup. Maybe the final step is a trap the PCs have to step into, or desperately try to find a way around - a killzone set up around the ship or what have you. The important part is that the plan has been presented, the PCs are trapped in it, and they have time to stew. I think the ship is a good set for that. Maybe the hunters have kept control of the deck and are just waiting there until the vampires walk into their lines of fire or the sun rises. Maybe they're doing that and they've got demons stalking the lower decks and/or driving the players down there(thanks castigation) and they're casting the ship off while they're squatting up top all prepared, so if the players don't escape soon they'll be stuck far out at sea with nothing to eat.<br /> <br /> Whatever the mechanism, make the players feel like they almost got railroaded - not so much by your fiat as by the hunters being very, very prepared - and got out by the skin of their teeth, but the train's gonna come back and run them over.<br /> <br /> The other thing I'd emphasize is <b>reversal</b>. Hunters flip the script. They're not so much about rising tension so much as a sudden panicking spike of revelation when the monsters realize they're not in control like they thought. However they get the PCs onto the ship should play to that - there's a temptation of food, or a supposed troubled innocent, or whatever lure, and it's difficult to realize they're being played until that plan's already swinging into action. Or maybe they pretend to be much less dangerous hunters, and 'run away' onto the ship, and only then does their planning and demonic heritage come into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T01:51:55-07:00","id":621959,"title":"","content":"As you have an enclosed, hard to navigate area <a href=\"http://tuckerskobolds.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Tucker's Kobolds</a> seem like prime inspiration here. Emphasize how the Hunters had time to prepare the area and make the entire ship into a death trap.<br /> <br /> Sidenote: If you have a PC that has some power that makes them resistant to fear this entire situation could be used to emphasize this. With the WoD's focus on personal horror this is a good chance to show how inhuman it is to be so unaffected by the horror of the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T17:49:23-07:00","id":622923,"title":"","content":"One thing that works really well for me, is to do a slow reveal. Don't give the farm up right away and announce who's cornered them. The PCs don't have to know that they're facing off Hunters in the middle of a trap, and you can play around with their expectations and assumptions while they try to escape. Too, if the PCs aren't tech-savvy, I would use that against them. Or, in other words, use their lack of knowledge about modern day humans against them. Let the Hunters use what the PCs don't, and that should scare the crap out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T19:03:13-07:00","id":629399,"title":"","content":"Shock and Awe: have a seemingly untouchable NPC get 1-shotted out of nowhere. That'll rattle your players pretty quick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T19:58:47-07:00","id":629413,"title":"","content":"Make it scary to stop them. <br /> <br /> Not as in &quot;they're almost impossible to kill&quot;, but demonstrate their attachment to their communities. Show all the lives they're fighting for. Show what will happen when those hunters are no longer around. Show what other, worse monsters are being held at bay by their existence. <br /> <br /> Human drama is one of the scariest things a monster can face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T20:51:53-07:00","id":629477,"title":"","content":"1) Make them clever as hell. Plan things out how you would take on targets like your PC's group or the NPC's you're going after. Plan out multiple offshoots of possibilities based on what they know. Nothing is more terrifying than realize the story you were carving in with fear was actually strains of the symphony they composed.<br /> <br /> 2) Exploit the chinks. If yer hunter group is watching and paying enough attention, they should have a portfolio of failings and reliances that the monsters are displaying. Take damn advantage of that. Don't just push these buttons, jam them in and then break the board.<br /> <br /> 3) Keep them invisible. Monica already hit on this, but consider that most supernaturals are good at finding their own, but only some are good at finding others. It's not a hard rule, course (werewolves), but basically hunters can blend into the flock and take advantage of those possibilities. Humans actually have a lot of ways they are inherently invisible, and playing with that will give you the edge you need.<br /> <br /> 4) Worth remembering is that hunters <i>aren't</i> distracted by the pursuit of the occult or extensions of natural abilities-even the Conspiracies aren't always as wholly distracted by the pursuit of esoteric powers as monsters are. So, don't be afraid to push that &quot;I'm more skilled than you&quot; button. While the werewolf's busy picking up Gifts or the Changeling is digging up Contracts, the hunter is becoming a better, well, hunter.<br /> <br /> 5) Keep the Desperation strong with their level of involvment. Hunters don't nessecarily hop to suicide bombing and molotoving all over the place, but by knowing the people in the cell and knowing what their outer limits are, you can make it clear that the person is pushing the edge of what they believe to be reasonable. Hunters are scary because running the knife's edge is their freaking modus operandi, rather than an occcasional fallback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T20:57:52-07:00","id":629480,"title":"","content":"Give your players something worth fighting for. <br /> <br /> Look to Shakespeare. <br /> <br /> If you draw the hunters in REAL close before letting the players in on what you're doing, it can be immensely hard to kill without massive, even potentially life-ending consequences. If Romeo loves Juliet, it's that much harder to actually rise up and kill Tybalt. It becomes a huge deal, beyond just some health levels. <br /> <br /> A good example of this is in MTV's Teen Wolf. The protagonist, a werewolf, falls in love with a young woman who is part of a family of monster hunters. Neither knows at the time. But, as this becomes a thing, both characters have to struggle with it. Could he just kill the family? Probably. But the director, the writer put faces on them. They made the hunters human. Killing real, relatable people is hard as fuck. <br /> <br /> So if you want to make them scary, make your players not wonder IF they can kill them, but SHOULD they.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T21:24:44-07:00","id":629544,"title":"","content":"This is true. Fighting for your life isn't a terrible narrative, but it's not the best one to go with in most case. Conflict with hunters should be at load-bearing narrative points about to bust if it goes wrong, more so than usual with antagonists because, if nothing else, hunters look for those sorts of moments and circumstances to strike at because it gives them a big advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T02:38:37-07:00","id":629742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) Keep the Desperation strong with their level of involvment. Hunters don't nessecarily hop to suicide bombing and molotoving all over the place, but by knowing the people in the cell and knowing what their outer limits are, you can make it clear that the person is pushing the edge of what they believe to be reasonable. Hunters are scary because running the knife's edge is their freaking modus operandi, rather than an occcasional fallback. </div> </div> </div>That's true in a narrative sense, but I find it conflicts with the fact that this is a game of make-believe. The extreme behaviour of NPCs can very easily just drive players to their own extreme behaviour, and generally as you're still trying to keep a degree of plausibility in the world you've created, the players are going to be much worse that the NPCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if you want to make them scary, make your players not wonder IF they can kill them, but SHOULD they. </div> </div> </div>Is that scary though? I've run stuff like that myself, and it's great drama, but I wouldn't call it scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T05:47:18-07:00","id":629822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/620855-need-tips-on-making-hunters-scary-to-be-stalked-by-if-you-re-a-monster?p=629742#post629742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that scary though? I've run stuff like that myself, and it's great drama, but I wouldn't call it scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's scary to lose a loved one, be it directly, or by alienating him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:35:32-07:00","id":629851,"title":"","content":"Sure, in real life it is. But this is fiction, and I don't think it translates, there's too much distance. Romeo and Juliet is tragic, it isn't scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:42:53-07:00","id":629855,"title":"","content":"Its terrifying when your home is invaded. Of having them know where your loved ones are, the things you hold dear. Don't fear for yourself. Fear for others. <br /> <br /> Be afraid of alerting the Hunter's police connections. Just because you can easily kill a hunter when you're one of the monsters doesn't mean the backlash won't be terrible. <br /> <br /> Hunters generally aren't afraid of going to extreme lengths to take on the supernatural. The supernatural, ironically, tend to have more restraint (save when we're talking about things like the Brood, Seers, and the Bale Hounds). In a game of chicken, the hunters will generally have more guts to stay the course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/620855-need-tips-on-making-hunters-scary-to-be-stalked-by-if-you-re-a-monster?p=629742#post629742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that scary though? I've run stuff like that myself, and it's great drama, but I wouldn't call it scary.</div> </div> </div> </div> Try the knife trick, where you try to stab between your fingers without cutting yourself. Pretty scary to go through with. Emotions, like fear of hurting a loved one, aren't less real or scary than stabbing your hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:44:12-07:00","id":629858,"title":"","content":"Depending on how well established the Hunters are, I think you draw upon the fact that the Hunters are likely to be well informed, well funded, well equipped and well organized.<br /> <br /> The PC's wont be fighting 5 random dudes with guns. They're being stalked by 5 trained killers, backed and funded by a world spanning organization of other trained killers. They know where you live, where you work, where you go to get drunk and where you shit. You're never safe. You can never let your guard down.<br /> Hunters are ruthless, relentless and resourceful. Use that. Have them burn the PC's houses, send them pictures of their loved ones homes, get them fired or put in jail on false accusations of rape or pedophillia, hack their bank accounts, rig their cars with bombs the list is infinite.<br /> The actual &quot;they're gonna kill us&quot;-part is just facet of the sustained and coordinated campaign of terror that a Hunter is likely to unleash to take down a powerful supernatural foe. Even when they do come for the kill, they're not gonna walk to you with a knife and slash away. They're gonna be sitting half a mile away, with sniper rifles and machine guns and you're in a wide open field, because you were lured there by the Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:47:53-07:00","id":629865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/620855-need-tips-on-making-hunters-scary-to-be-stalked-by-if-you-re-a-monster?p=629851#post629851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, in real life it is. But this is fiction, and I don't think it translates, there's too much distance. Romeo and Juliet is tragic, it isn't scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you're the reader. It's scary for Romeo and Juliet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T08:10:34-07:00","id":629956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/620855-need-tips-on-making-hunters-scary-to-be-stalked-by-if-you-re-a-monster?p=629742#post629742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's true in a narrative sense, but I find it conflicts with the fact that this is a game of make-believe. The extreme behaviour of NPCs can very easily just drive players to their own extreme behaviour, and generally as you're still trying to keep a degree of plausibility in the world you've created, the players are going to be much worse that the NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly this is where the Morality/Integrity system comes in. Not to &quot;punish&quot; certain behavior mind you, but to bring out the effect of the social contract in game where player's might be inclined to disregard it because of their separation (being real rather than the fictional characters) from the consequences. A Hunter who is comfortable with easy murder should have fairly low Integrity and run the risk of scratching at Slasher impulses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T08:57:53-07:00","id":629975,"title":"","content":"Problems based on a game being make believe are only a problem <i>if you refuse to make believe</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T01:07:16-07:00","id":630792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/620855-need-tips-on-making-hunters-scary-to-be-stalked-by-if-you-re-a-monster?p=629399#post629399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shock and Awe: have a seemingly untouchable NPC get 1-shotted out of nowhere. That'll rattle your players pretty quick.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a fine line between making it scary, and making the players just feel frustrated and hopeless. The first is fine, the second is just going to ruin the game for the people at your table. Besides, if you one shot a NPC, and then cannot do the same with the characters in the same situation, you tend to harm their suspension of disbelief. At the same time, no player is going to like to be killed by a rock from the sky either. Unless you have a pretty good reason for why that one shot kill worked, and why it only worked once (and the characters learn the reasons), there is in my experience a pretty big chance such tactics backfire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:15:40-07:00","id":631198,"title":"","content":"Tactics. Corollary to the 'go after the money' from earlier, most hunters are fully aware that they're not going to win a toe-to-toe without serious hardware. So they do things differently. One thing I'm fond of is 'poisoning the food.' Vampires, particularly well-established ones, don't think too much about feeding. If a vampire goes to feed and gets his brains splattered across an alleyway, then suddenly the rules have changed. My favorite setting I ever did for a Vampire game was a Ventrue prince who used the Masquerade as a McCarthy-style bludgeon -- anything bad happens in the city? Must be a breach, sanctions for everybody. If a hunter kills a neonate somewhere and <i>the entire metropolitan infrastructure reacts</i>, that's a pretty good indication some serious shit went down.<br /> <br /> Also on the matter of tactics, 'divide and conquer' is a good one. If the PCs' allies start coming after them, murder in their eyes, the PCs are like as not curious as to why. Let them investigate, and discover that the hunters have been working on a frame job, and PCs' allies were suckered. That does a really good job of establishing what kind of juice hunters have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7353-voragosolitude","name":"VoragoSolitude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7353_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T14:02:16-07:00","id":631536,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this was mentioned already, but there's a chapter dedicated to hunters-as-enemies in the Antagonists splatbook for 1e; in addition to the advice here, I highly recommend checking it out.<br /> <br /> Something to remember is that, since your group are playing supernats, the best way to play up hunters as antagonists is to avoid the &quot;whitewashing&quot; they get given in their own gameline. Hunters who actually <i>hunt</i> are desperate, vicious, and half-deranged. These are the hunters who <b>will</b> send the PC threatening notes and incriminating pictures. They <b>will</b> torture and murder the PCs friends, family and lovers for information or just to terrorize the PCs.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, being stalked by hunters should feel like being stalked by a serial killer, or living out a slasher movie. Because, from a supernat's perspective, that's what hunters are.<br /> <br /> Use traps, ambush, headgames, hit and run, try to drive them into a killzone or whittle them down in order to make them vulnerable to a final attack. If one player (or a cannon fodder NPC) falls, emphasize the brutal violence of their death, especially at the hands of the hunters proper. If your players are willing to play along with this, that should really help drive the horror home.<br /> <br /> That said, don't be afraid to embrace it if the PCs lash out. The fear response is called fight or flight for a reason, and supernats have a lot of options to fight. If possible, show them how dangerous just blindly fighting is - but, if they win, then use that to drive home that they are still <i>monsters</i>. Describe the visceral slaughter left in their wake, have dying hunters plead and babble apologies to their loved ones... let them feel ashamed at how readily they have reduced living, breathing beings to so much cooling meat.<br /> <br /> Then slap them with the realisation: what do we do now? Gotta get rid of the bodies, or doctor them, or else the law will come after them.<br /> <br /> But, ultimately, be prepared for players to not play along. Even in a horror game, many players don't like <i>like</i> to feel helpless, particularly when it's something that they &quot;know&quot; they can deal with. There's a fine line between horror and nihilistic frustration; push some players too far, and they'll deliberately lash out, ruining your planned scene because they would rather your NPCs burn with them rather than lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T14:15:09-07:00","id":632713,"title":"","content":"There's some good conversations here, and I would add that it might be worth thinking about expected vs. unexpected outcomes. For example, if the Hunters understand what the monsters fear, is that part of their trap? Say their plan, all along, is to frighten the monsters so badly they bear claws/fangs. Why? Is it to study them? Is it because they'd been hunting them for months? Is it to trap or doublecross (e.g. Draw in a second monster type to have them kill each other.) them? Right now, it sounds to me like the expected outcome is a big battle. I'm suggesting that it doesn't have to be that simple, and that might give you other options to introduce Hunters as an antagonist. Too, there are monsters that throw their lot in with Hunters on occasion to fight monsters. This could draw some connections between the PCs and the NPCs in an interesting way. So to sum up: I'd think about motivation, because depending upon why the Hunters are going after your PCs, that has the ability to make your scenario pop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T18:49:13-07:00","id":632945,"title":"","content":"My proposal... First contact has the players and hunters BOTH on the SAME SIDE. <br /> <br /> And during that point, you show them do things like have a willingness to do acts that bother your players. Maybe they call in an airstrike against a sludge monster and are armed to the teeth... or are flatout inhuman in their actions, such as playing the zealotry and conviction to terrifying levels. Let them have harsh treatment of the first bad guy's cultists, let them cut down those involved but unaware. And show them how dedicated and willing they are to throw themselves into the line of fire to achieve their goals. They're a different sort of inhuman then.<br /> <br /> If it works, they'll hesitate fighting them. And if you go far enough, be scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}